  "question": {
    "text": "One of the two identical conducting wires of length <math><mi>L</mi></math> is bent in the form of a circular loop and the other one into a circular coil of <math><mi>N</mi></math> identical turns. If the same current is passed in both, the ratio of the magnetic field at the centre of the loop <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> to that at the centre of the coil <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> i.e. <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gXFU4",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
